## Direct Recommendation

Make `CanvaViewer` a **controlled, commit-based editor**: canvas edits are held in a `pendingText` buffer and only pushed upstream when the user clicks **Save**. **Discard** forces `<CanvaEditor>` to rebuild from the last saved definition. `Code.vue` already wires `@change` → `codeText` → `rebuildMarkdownText()` → `text-changed`, so saving is all that's needed to update both the JSON code block **and** the chat message.

## Why this approach

- **Single source of truth for persistence:** the canvas is a *draft*; the code block is the *document*. Never auto-write drafts to disk.
- **Zero changes in `Code.vue`:** its `onCanvaChange` handler already updates `codeText` and emits `text-changed`, which is the exact path used to persist the chat message.
- **Reliable discard:** assigning a *fresh array reference* to `nodes` re-triggers the deep watcher in `CanvaEditor`, forcing a full `loadJsonToCanvas` rebuild without emitting a change (guarded by its own `isUpdatingFromProp`).

## Specifications

| Dimension | Decision |
|---|---|
| **State** | `savedText` (committed) · `pendingText` (draft) · `dirty` (computed) |
| **Toolbar** | Only rendered when `dirty` — avoids visual noise on read-only views |
| **Save** | `savedText = pendingText`, clear draft, `$emit('change', savedText)` |
| **Discard** | Clear draft, reload editor from `savedText` via new array reference |
| **Colors** | `bg-base-200` bar, `border-base-100`, `bg-warning` status dot, `btn-primary` CTA |
| **UX states** | Buttons are DaisyUI `btn-xs`, keyboard focusable, labelled |

---

```vue src/components/canva/CanvaViewer.vue
<script setup>
import CanvaEditor from './CanvaEditor.vue'
</script>

<template>
  <!--
    Inline preview/editor of a `canva` code block.

    The stored definition is a JSON string, but <CanvaEditor> works with a plain
    node array. This wrapper parses one into the other and keeps every visual
    change PENDING until the user decides:

    - Save:    bubbles the new definition up through `change` so the consumer
               updates the code block (and the chat message).
    - Discard: reloads the last saved definition and drops the pending edits.

    A fixed (resizable) height is required because chat blocks are inline and
    <CanvaEditor> itself expands to `h-full`.
  -->
  <div class="w-full rounded-lg border border-base-100 bg-base-300 overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Unsaved changes toolbar -->
    <div
      class="flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-2 border-b border-base-100 bg-base-200"
      v-if="dirty"
    >
      <span class="text-xs opacity-60 mr-auto flex items-center gap-1.5">
        <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-warning"></span>
        Unsaved changes
      </span>
      <button class="btn btn-xs btn-ghost" @click="discard">
        Discard
      </button>
      <button class="btn btn-xs btn-primary" @click="save">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-floppy-disk"></i>
        Save
      </button>
    </div>

    <div class="w-full h-96 min-h-64 max-h-[80vh] resize-y overflow-hidden">
      <CanvaEditor
        class="w-full h-full"
        :modelValue="nodes"
        @update:modelValue="onCanvasUpdate"
      />
    </div>
  </div>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  name: 'CanvaViewer',
  props: {
    // Raw canva definition stored in the code block. Accepts both a root array
    // of nodes and the { nodes: [...] } envelope used by `.canva` files.
    text: {
      type: String,
      default: ''
    }
  },
  emits: ['change'],
  data() {
    return {
      // Parsed definition handed to <CanvaEditor>. Only replaced on external
      // changes so canvas edits never wipe the workspace.
      nodes: [],
      // Canonical encoding of the definition that is currently persisted.
      savedText: null,
      // Canonical encoding of the edits made on the canvas but not saved yet.
      pendingText: null
    }
  },
  computed: {
    // There are canvas edits that were not committed yet.
    dirty() {
      return this.pendingText !== null && this.pendingText !== this.savedText
    }
  },
  created() {
    this.savedText = this.text || null
    this.nodes = this.parseDefinition(this.text)
  },
  watch: {
    text(newText) {
      // Ignore the echo of the change we just emitted after saving.
      if ((newText || null) === this.savedText) return
      this.savedText = newText || null
      this.pendingText = null
      this.nodes = this.parseDefinition(newText)
    }
  },
  methods: {
    // Accept both a root array and a { nodes: [...] } envelope
    parseDefinition(content) {
      if (!content) return []
      try {
        const parsed = JSON.parse(content)
        return Array.isArray(parsed) ? parsed : (parsed.nodes || [])
      } catch (ex) {
        console.warn('Invalid canva definition', ex)
        return []
      }
    },
    // Canvas changed: hold the new definition as pending so the user decides
    // when it is persisted through Save.
    onCanvasUpdate(nodes) {
      this.pendingText = JSON.stringify({ nodes }, null, 2)
    },
    // Commit the pending definition. The consumer is responsible for updating
    // the code block (and the chat message) with the emitted JSON.
    save() {
      if (!this.dirty) return
      this.savedText = this.pendingText
      this.pendingText = null
      this.$emit('change', this.savedText)
    },
    // Drop the pending edits and reload the last saved definition. A fresh array
    // reference forces <CanvaEditor> to rebuild its workspace.
    discard() {
      this.pendingText = null
      this.nodes = [...this.parseDefinition(this.savedText)]
    }
  }
}
</script>
```

## Flow (end-to-end)

```
Canvas drag ──▶ CanvaEditor @update:modelValue
                └─▶ CanvaViewer.pendingText  (dirty = true, toolbar shows)
                        │
        ┌───────────────┴────────────────┐
        ▼ Save                           ▼ Discard
  emit('change', JSON)            nodes = fresh copy
        │                                └─▶ CanvaEditor reloads saved state
        ▼
  Code.vue.onCanvaChange(newContent)
        └─▶ this.codeText = newContent
            this.rebuildMarkdownText()
              └─▶ $emit('text-changed', …)
                    └─▶ chat message persisted ✅
```

## Change Summary

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `src/components/canva/CanvaViewer.vue` | Added pending/dirty buffering + Save/Discard toolbar; changes are no longer auto-emitted on every canvas update. |
| `src/components/Code.vue` | **No change** — its existing `onCanvaChange` already updates the JSON block and calls `rebuildMarkdownText()` to update the chat message. |

## Anti-Patterns Avoided

- ❌ **Auto-writing the draft on every drag** — floods the message with `text-changed` events and makes the code block jittery during editing.
- ❌ **Reloading the canvas after Save** — keeps selection/undo intact; the canvas *is* the new saved state, so no reload is needed (only `savedText` is updated).
- ❌ **Overriding active edits with prop echoes** — the `newText === savedText` guard prevents the parent's echoed prop from resetting the workspace.

## Accessibility Checklist

- [x] Save/Discard are real `<button>` elements (Tab-reachable, Enter/Space activatable).
- [x] Text labels precede icons ("Save", "Discard") — no icon-only ambiguity.
- [x] Status uses both a colour dot **and** the text "Unsaved changes" (no colour-only meaning).
- [x] DaisyUI `btn` tokens carry the standard visible `focus-visible` ring.
- [x] Toolbar renders only when actionable — no dead controls in the tab order.

## Implementation Steps

1. Replace `src/components/canva/CanvaViewer.vue` with the file above.
2. Verify `Code.vue` still passes `:text="codeText"` and `@change="onCanvaChange"` (unchanged).
3. **Test:** open a chat with a `canva` block → drag a shape → toolbar appears → click **Discard** (canvas reverts) → drag again → click **Save** → the code block JSON and the chat message both update.
4. **Test edge case:** reload the chat — the saved JSON should re-render identically in the canvas.

Got it — right now an **empty** canva block never opens the editor, because `isValidCanva` is `false` when there is no content, so `showCanvaEditor` stays `false` and you only see the empty code block. Let's let an empty block open a **blank** canvas, while keeping the source fallback for *broken* JSON.

## Change

Only `src/components/Code.vue` changes. I split the current `isValidCanva`-gated logic into two concepts:

| Concept | Meaning | Used for |
|---|---|---|
| `canvaHasContent` | The block has non-whitespace text | Tell "blank start" apart from "broken JSON" |
| `canvaEditorAvailable` | A valid definition **or** an empty block | Show the canvas (blank when empty) |

Behavior matrix:

| Block content | Result |
|---|---|
| empty / whitespace | Editor opens **blank**; "View source" toggles to the fence |
| valid JSON (`[…]` or `{ nodes: […] }`) | Editor opens with the definition (as today) |
| invalid JSON | Editor **not** shown → source view (so it can be fixed) |

```vue src/components/Code.vue
<script setup>
import MermaidViewerVue from './MermaidViewer.vue'
import MarkdownViewer from './MarkdownViewer.vue'
import CodeViewer from './CodeViewer.vue'
import HTMLPreview from './HTMLPreview.vue'
import BlockEditor from './BlockEditor.vue'
import CanvaViewer from './canva/CanvaViewer.vue'
</script>

<template>
  <BlockEditor
    :originalContent="codeText"
    :isCodeBlock="!showMarkdown"
    :language="language"
    ref="blockEditor"
    @edit-start="onEditStart"
    @edit-cancel="onEditCancel"
    @edit-save="onEditSave"
  >
    <div class="rounded-md py-2">
      <!-- Edit button (shown on hover) -->
      <div
        class="absolute -left-10 top-0 opacity-0 hover:opacity-100 transition-opacity"
        v-if="!isEditing"
      >
        <button
          class="btn btn-xs btn-ghost tooltip tooltip-right"
          data-tip="Edit block"
          @click="startEdit"
        >
          <i class="fa-solid fa-pen"></i>
        </button>
      </div>

      <div class="flex gap-2 w-full justify-end rounded-t" ref="toolbar" v-if="(showMermaid || showHTMLPreview || showCanva) && !isEditing">
        <button class="btn btn-xs" @click="showMermaidSource = !showMermaidSource" v-if="showMermaid">
          <span v-if="showMermaidSource">View diagram</span>
          <span v-else>View code</span>
        </button>
        <button class="btn btn-sm bg-info/60 my-2 flex gap-2" @click="htmlPreview = !htmlPreview" v-if="showHTMLPreview">
          <span v-if="htmlPreview">View code</span>
          <span v-else><i class="fa-solid fa-tablet-screen-button"></i> View preview</span>
        </button>
        <button class="btn btn-sm bg-info/60 my-2 flex gap-2" @click="showCanvaSource = !showCanvaSource" v-if="showCanva && canvaEditorAvailable">
          <span v-if="showCanvaSource"><i class="fa-solid fa-palette"></i> View canvas</span>
          <span v-else><i class="fa-solid fa-code"></i> View source</span>
        </button>
      </div>

      <MermaidViewerVue
        :diagram="codeText"
        theme="dark"
        @click="showMermaidSource = !showMermaidSource"
        v-if="showMermaid && !showMermaidSource && !isEditing"
      />

      <HTMLPreview
        :html="codeText"
        v-if="showHTMLPreview && htmlPreview && !isEditing"
      />

      <CanvaViewer
        :text="codeText"
        @change="onCanvaChange"
        v-if="showCanvaEditor && !isEditing"
      />

      <CodeViewer
        :code="codeText"
        :language="language"
        :file="file"
        :files="files"
        :project="project"
        :finished="finished"
        :chat="chat"
        :message="message"
        :key="blockHash"
        v-if="showCode && !isEditing"
        @reload-file="$emit('reload-file', $event)"
        @open-file="$emit('open-file', $event)"
        @save-file="$emit('save-file', $event)"
        @add-file="$emit('add-file', $event)"
        @sub-task="$emit('sub-task', $event)"
        @message-change="onMessageChange"
      />

      <MarkdownViewer :text="codeText" v-if="showMarkdown && !isEditing" />
    </div>
  </BlockEditor>
</template>

<script>
const languageMapping = {
  "vue": "html",
  "markdown": "md",
  "html": "html"
}

export default {
  props: ['chat', 'finished', 'code', 'text', 'text-language', 'file-name', 'files', 'project', 'message', 'block-hash'],
  emits: ['reload-file', 'open-file', 'save-file', 'add-file', 'sub-task', 'edit-message', 'generate-code', 'text-changed', 'block-edited'],
  data() {
    return {
      codeText: null,
      languages: null,
      htmlPreview: false,
      showMermaidSource: false,
      showCanvaSource: false,
      file: null,
      previousText: null,
      isEditing: false
    }
  },
  created() {
    const language = languageMapping[this.codeLanguage] || this.codeLanguage
    this.languages = [[language, language.toUpperCase()]]
    this.codeText = this.text || this.code?.innerText
    this.file = this.fileName || this.code?.attributes["data-file"]?.value
    this.previousText = this.codeText
  },
  mounted() {
    if (this.code) {
      this.code?.parentNode.after(this.$el)
      this.code?.parentNode.remove()
      this.$bubble('code-file-shown', { somedata: true })
    }
  },
  computed: {
    isVibeCoding() {
      return this.chat?.mode === 'vibe'
    },
    language() {
      const lang = this.textLanguage ||
        this.code?.attributes["class"]?.value.split("-").reverse()[0]
      return languageMapping[lang] || lang
    },
    codeLanguage() {
      return this.language?.includes("mermaid") ? "markdown" : this.language
    },
    showMermaid() {
      return this.language === 'mermaid' && !this.isVibeCoding
    },
    showHTMLPreview() {
      const extension = this.fileName?.split(".")[1] || this.codeLanguage
      return ['html'].includes(extension) && !this.isVibeCoding
    },
    showCanva() {
      return this.language === 'canva' && !this.isVibeCoding
    },
    // The block carries actual content (blank/whitespace blocks start empty)
    canvaHasContent() {
      return !!(this.codeText && this.codeText.trim())
    },
    isValidCanva() {
      if (!this.codeText) return false
      try {
        const parsed = JSON.parse(this.codeText)
        if (Array.isArray(parsed)) return true
        return !!(parsed && Array.isArray(parsed.nodes))
      } catch (ex) {
        return false
      }
    },
    // The canvas can be opened when there is a valid definition to load OR the
    // block is empty (in which case the editor starts blank so it can be drawn
    // from scratch). A block with broken JSON is NOT openable, so its source is
    // shown instead and can be fixed.
    canvaEditorAvailable() {
      return this.isValidCanva || !this.canvaHasContent
    },
    showCanvaEditor() {
      return this.showCanva && !this.showCanvaSource && this.canvaEditorAvailable
    },
    showCode() {
      return !this.showMarkdown && (!this.showMermaid || this.showMermaidSource) && (!this.showHTMLPreview || !this.htmlPreview) && !this.showCanvaEditor
    },
    showMarkdown() {
      return this.language === 'md' && !this.fileName
    },
    codeBlockInfo() {
      return {
        code: this.text || this.code?.innerText,
        language: this.language
      }
    }
  },
  watch: {
    text(newVal) {
      if (newVal !== undefined && newVal !== this.codeText) {
        this.previousText = this.codeText
        this.codeText = newVal
      }
    },
    code(newCode) {
      if (newCode?.innerText !== undefined) {
        const innerText = newCode.innerText
        if (innerText !== this.codeText) {
          this.previousText = this.codeText
          this.codeText = innerText
        }
      }
    }
  },
  methods: {
    startEdit() {
      this.isEditing = true
      this.$refs.blockEditor.startEdit()
    },
    onEditStart() {
      this.isEditing = true
    },
    onEditCancel() {
      this.isEditing = false
    },
    onEditSave({ originalContent, newContent }) {
      this.isEditing = false
      this.codeText = newContent
      this.$emit('block-edited', {
        originalContent,
        newContent,
        blockHash: this.blockHash,
        language: this.language
      })
      this.rebuildMarkdownText()
    },
    onMessageChange({ orgContent, newContent }) {
      this.codeText = newContent
      this.rebuildMarkdownText()
    },
    onCanvaChange(newContent) {
      this.codeText = newContent
      this.rebuildMarkdownText()
    },
    rebuildMarkdownText() {
      const siblings = this.$parent?.$children?.filter(c => c.$options?.name === undefined
        ? false
        : c.codeText !== undefined) || []

      if (!siblings.length) {
        this.$emit('text-changed', this.buildFence(this.codeText))
        return
      }

      this.$emit('text-changed', { block: this, newContent: this.codeText })
    },
    buildFence(content) {
      const lang = this.language || ''
      const fileHint = this.file ? ` ${this.file}` : ''
      return `\`\`\`${lang}${fileHint}\n${content}\n\`\`\``
    }
  }
}
</script>
```

## Test flow with your empty block

```
┌ canva block (empty) ─────────────┐
│  canvaHasContent = false         │
│  canvaEditorAvailable = true     │
│  → CanvaViewer opens BLANK ✅     │
└──────────────────────────────────┘
      │ draw a shape
      ▼
  CanvaEditor @update:modelValue → pendingText   (dirty → toolbar shows)
      │ Save
      ▼
  $emit('change', '{"nodes":[…] }')
      ▼
  Code.onCanvaChange → codeText = JSON → rebuildMarkdownText() → text-changed
      │
      ▼
  isValidCanva now true → "View source" toggle appears ✅
```

## Notes

- **No changes needed in `CanvaViewer.vue` / `CanvaEditor.vue`.** `CanvaViewer.parseDefinition('')` already returns `[]`, and `CanvaEditor.loadJsonToCanvas([])` clears the workspace → blank canvas. The `save()`/`discard()` flow is unchanged.
- **Broken JSON stays editable as source** — we deliberately do **not** blank-slate invalid non-empty content, otherwise a user typo would silently wipe their definition the moment they drew on it.

