## 1. Analysis & Pre-Thinking

**Core Requirements**
- When the user clicks **Save** in the canva view, the underlying code block must be rewritten in the chat message and persisted.
- Only the `canva` fenced block may change; all other message content (text, other code blocks) must stay intact.
- The update must go through the chat store.

**Component chain (message path)**
```
Chat.vue → ChatMessageList → ChatEntry → document/Document.vue → ChapterBlock.vue → Code.vue → canva/CanvaViewer.vue → canva/CanvaEditor.vue
```
- `CanvaViewer` already implements **Save/Discard** and only emits `change` (on Save) with the new JSON string. ✅ (no change needed)
- `Code.vue` receives `@change="onCanvaChange"`, sets `codeText`, then calls `rebuildMarkdownText()` which emits `text-changed`… **but no ancestor in the message path listens to `text-changed`** — that's exactly why the message never updates.
- `Code.vue` already has both `:chat` and `:message` props (passed by `ChapterBlock`), so it can update the owning message directly.

**Strategic Approach**
1. In `Code.vue`, when a canva block belongs to a chat message (`chat` + `message` present), rebuild the message content by replacing **only** the matching `canva` fenced block, then call the chat store. Otherwise keep the old `text-changed` flow.
2. Add a focused `updateMessageContent` action to the chat store that locates the message, updates its `content`, and persists it through the existing `updateMessage` action.

**Dependencies & Risks**
- The message block renders with a synthetic file name (`content.canva`), so matching by the rendered fence header is unreliable → match the fenced `canva` block by **language + body equality** (with a plain body-replace fallback).
- Multiple canva blocks in one message: matched by exact body, so only the correct one is replaced.
- `previousText` already tracks the last block content, so it is the correct "old" value to locate.

**Target Files**
- `src/components/Code.vue` — Modify (`onCanvaChange`, add `saveCanvaToMessage`, `replaceCanvaBlock`)
- `src/store/chats.js` — Modify (add `updateMessageContent` action)
- `src/components/canva/CanvaViewer.vue` — No change (Save/Discard + `change` emit already present)
- `src/components/canva/CanvaEditor.vue` — No change (already emits `update:modelValue`)

## 2. Minimum Changes Approach

1. **`src/components/Code.vue`** → `onCanvaChange` now persists to the message via the store; two new helper methods (`saveCanvaToMessage`, `replaceCanvaBlock`).
2. **`src/store/chats.js`** → new `updateMessageContent` action.

No changes to `CanvaViewer.vue`/`CanvaEditor.vue` — the Save/Discard UI and the `change`/`update:modelValue` wiring already exist.

