## 4. File Change Summary

| File Path | Action | Component / Section | Change Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `src/components/Code.vue` | Modify | `onCanvaChange` | Routes the canva save to `saveCanvaToMessage` when the block belongs to a chat message (else keeps `text-changed`). |
| `src/components/Code.vue` | Modify | `saveCanvaToMessage` | Builds the updated message content (only the canva block changed) and persists it through the chat store. |
| `src/components/Code.vue` | Modify | `replaceCanvaBlock` | Replaces only the `canva` fenced block matching the previous body, with a plain-replace fallback. |
| `src/store/chats.js` | Modify | `updateMessageContent` | New action to update a single message's `content` and persist it. |
| `src/components/canva/CanvaViewer.vue` | No change | Save/Discard toolbar | Already implemented — emits `change` on Save, resets pending edits on Discard. |
| `src/components/canva/CanvaEditor.vue` | No change | `update:modelValue` | Already wires canvas edits up to the wrapper. |

### How it works now (flow)
1. User edits the canvas → `CanvaEditor` emits `update:modelValue` → `CanvaViewer` holds it as **pending**.
2. User clicks **Save** → `CanvaViewer.save()` emits `change` with the JSON.
3. `Code.onCanvaChange` → `saveCanvaToMessage`:
   - Locates and replaces **only** the matching `canva` fence inside `message.content`.
   - Updates the message in place (instant UI refresh) and calls `$storex.chats.updateMessageContent({ chat, doc_id, content })`.
4. The store updates the message and persists it; all other parts of the message remain untouched.
5. **Discard** simply drops pending edits and reloads the last saved definition (unchanged).

